course: dictionary
lesson: 7982
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning the writer wants. Recorder can be a musical instrument, a machine, or a person.
explain: «Blowing too hard makes a recorder jump up to a shrill squeal.» You blow into this recorder and cover its holes with your fingers, so it must be the instrument. Always check: does your meaning fit the sentence?
explain: «If something ever goes wrong in the air, two tough recorders called the black box help investigators find out why.» These recorders are machines that keep a record of sound and information. The clue is the air and the investigators.
fact: A recorder can be a musical instrument, a machine, or a person.
fact: A recorder, the instrument, is a simple wooden or plastic wind instrument with holes that you cover with your fingers.
fact: A recorder, the machine, records sound or pictures, like a voice recorder or a video recorder.
fact: Composers such as Bach, Handel and Vivaldi wrote music for the recorder.
fact: In group work, the recorder is the person who writes down the group's ideas.
exercise: «Blowing too hard makes a recorder jump up to a shrill squeal.» What kind of recorder is this? | *A wind instrument you blow into | A pipe for carrying water | A machine that records sound | A person who writes things down
exercise: In a group, the recorder writes down the group's ideas. What does the recorder do? | *Writes down what the group says and decides | Plays a tune on the recorder | Blows into the pipe | Records a video of the group
exercise: Which recorder is a machine? | A recorder in a music lesson | A recorder who writes the ideas down | *A voice recorder that keeps sound | A recorder that plays Bach
test: What do you cover with your fingers to play a recorder? | *The holes | The wheels | The screen | The buttons
test: Who is the recorder when a group is working together? | The one who plays the tune | The teacher | *The one who writes down the ideas | The loudest singer
exam: In «a voice recorder», what kind of recorder is it? | *A machine that records sound | A wooden tool for playing tunes | A musical instrument | A person who writes things down
